-- Deploy with the fierymud-rs wait_ticks -> wait_hours engine rename and 2026-10-15-wait-hours-scripts.sql (no alias is kept).
-- Authored help guides (generated by `fierylib seed help --emit-sql`).
-- Source: fierylib/data/help/*.md. Do not edit by hand; edit the markdown
-- and regenerate.
-- Idempotent: matches on the primary keyword ("HelpEntry" has no unique key),
-- overwriting a legacy entry with the same primary keyword; a re-run changes 0 rows
-- (the UPDATE is skipped when the row already matches).

-- lua-world: Lua API: World and Global Functions
DO $do$
DECLARE v_id integer;
BEGIN
  SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE keywords[1] = 'lua-world' ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    SELECT id INTO v_id FROM "HelpEntry" WHERE 'lua-world' = ANY(keywords) ORDER BY id LIMIT 1;
  END IF;
  IF v_id IS NULL THEN
    INSERT INTO "HelpEntry"
      (keywords, title, content, min_level, category, usage, source_file, updated_at)
    VALUES (
      ARRAY['lua-world', 'world', 'lua globals', 'globals', 'lua functions']::text[],
      'Lua API: World and Global Functions',
      $help$Globals every trigger can use (return type after ->). Wherever (zone, id) is
shown, in any lua-* topic, the key may also be one table: f({zone, id}) or
f({zone = Z, id = I}). A malformed key is an error.
  get_room(zone, id) -> Room|nil
  find_actor(keyword) -> Actor|nil      whole world, first match; keyword is a
                                        case-insensitive substring of name/keywords
  random(low, high) -> int              inclusive; use this, not math.random
  percent_chance(n) -> bool             true n percent of the time
  wait(seconds)                         pause the script, then continue; fractions ok
                                        (wait(0.2)), rounded to 0.1 s server ticks, min 0.1
  wait_hours(n)                         pause n game hours (75 real seconds each)
  wait_until(hour, minute)              pause until that game time (minute optional)
  allow_command()                       COMMAND triggers: let the typed command go ahead
                                        and keep running (DG `return 0`); a script that
                                        reaches wait() without it consumes the command
  run_room_trigger(zone, id)            run every trigger on that room; deferred
                                        to after the current script finishes
  print(...)                            captured, NOT shown to players here;
                                        use actor:send / room:send instead
  globals                               scratch table, empty on every fire
World queries (namespace "world"):
  world.count_mobiles(zone, id) -> int  world.count_objects(zone, id) -> int
  world.find_mobile(zone, id) -> Actor|nil
  world.destroy(handle)                 despawn a mob or item
Prototypes (no spawn): mobiles.template(zone, id), objects.template(zone, id)
  -> read-only Proto with .id .zone_id .name .shortdesc
Combat (self is the fighter): combat.engage(target)   combat.rescue(victim)
Abilities:
  skills.set_level(actor, name, level)    grant or set a skill
  skills.execute(caster, name, target?)   target is an Actor or a name string
  spells.cast(caster, name, target?, level?)
  Effect.Name                             constant for has_effect, e.g.
                                          actor:has_effect(Effect.Sanctuary)
Clock (namespace "time", read-only snapshot taken when the script starts):
  time.stamp          Unix seconds (use for throttling: now - last > 5)
  time.hour 0-23, time.minute, time.day, time.month, time.year
  time.month_name, time.season, time.is_night, time.is_day
  One game hour is about 75 real seconds.
Event globals (strings): speech (SPEECH, lowercased), cmd and args (COMMAND).
Lua standard libraries: string, table, math, utf8, coroutine (read-only copies),
plus pairs, ipairs, tostring, tonumber, type, select, pcall, error, assert.
Removed: os, io, debug, package, load, loadstring, loadfile, dofile.
require("name") loads a shared library script (Muditor Scripts > Libraries); it
returns the same value to every trigger, so return data and functions. Libraries
cannot wait() or wait_hours() at their top level. See fierymud-rs/docs/SCRIPTING.md.
Limits: about 5 million instructions per run, 64 MB memory.
Persistent variables: obj:setvar / getvar / clearvar on mobs, items and rooms;
quest variables on players (see help lua-actor). Mob and item variables are
saved to the database about every 10 seconds.
Timing: wait(n) is real seconds; wait_hours(n) is game hours (75 s each). A script parked in wait() is lost on server
restart, and errors raised after a wait are not reported in the error log.
Messages sent from Lua already end with a newline; do not add \r\n.$help$,
      100,
      'building',
      'get_room(zone, id) / find_actor(keyword) / wait(seconds) / wait_hours(n)',
      'data/help/lua-world.md',
      now()
    );
  ELSE
    UPDATE "HelpEntry" SET
      keywords = ARRAY['lua-world', 'world', 'lua globals', 'globals', 'lua functions']::text[],
      title = 'Lua API: World and Global Functions',
      content = $help$Globals every trigger can use (return type after ->). Wherever (zone, id) is
shown, in any lua-* topic, the key may also be one table: f({zone, id}) or
f({zone = Z, id = I}). A malformed key is an error.
  get_room(zone, id) -> Room|nil
  find_actor(keyword) -> Actor|nil      whole world, first match; keyword is a
                                        case-insensitive substring of name/keywords
  random(low, high) -> int              inclusive; use this, not math.random
  percent_chance(n) -> bool             true n percent of the time
  wait(seconds)                         pause the script, then continue; fractions ok
                                        (wait(0.2)), rounded to 0.1 s server ticks, min 0.1
  wait_hours(n)                         pause n game hours (75 real seconds each)
  wait_until(hour, minute)              pause until that game time (minute optional)
  allow_command()                       COMMAND triggers: let the typed command go ahead
                                        and keep running (DG `return 0`); a script that
                                        reaches wait() without it consumes the command
  run_room_trigger(zone, id)            run every trigger on that room; deferred
                                        to after the current script finishes
  print(...)                            captured, NOT shown to players here;
                                        use actor:send / room:send instead
  globals                               scratch table, empty on every fire
